            <div xml:id="d160">

                <pb facs="0267" n="169" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg169"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">813.00/965</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Salvador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Arnold</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-06-25"><hi rendition="#italic">June 25,
                        1920</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received July 8.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 638</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my telegram No. 25 of June 25,
                    1920, 9 A.M.,<anchor n="36" xml:id="d160-f1"/> regarding a circular telegram
                    which was sent June 24th by the Salvadorian Government to the Chancelleries of
                    the Central American Republics inviting them to send delegates to a convention
                    to be held in order to discuss the questions pertaining to the Union of Central
                    America, I have the honor to enclose to the Department a copy of the circular
                    telegram with translation which was published in the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Diario Oficial</hi> of June 24, 1920.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank D. Arnold</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d160-a1.xml" xpointer="d160-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
